The term '''attacks per round''' (APR) refers to how many [[attack roll|attacks]] a [[creature]] is able to make during a [[round]] (6 seconds).  
The base attacks per round is determined by the creature's [[base attack bonus]] (BAB) &mdash; or [[unarmed base attack bonus]] (UBAB) in the case of a [[monk]] fighting unarmed or with a [[kama]].
Even though BAB continue to increase at epic levels, a character's maximum number of attacks is determined by his or her BAB at [[character level]] 20.

